*Note: Retail health GWP, Retail health market share, PAT (IFRS), and Claims ratio (IFRS) are not disclosed in the statutory filing and have been excluded from the table above per the sourcing rules (rather than estimated).*

## Key Notes & Data-Quality Flags

**PAT reconciliation:** The filing shows PAT = ₹(4,888) lakhs = **-₹48.88 crore** for the quarter ended 30-Jun-24 (vs. -₹36.39 crore in Q1FY24). This derives from an operating loss of ₹(5,695) lakhs from Health/Miscellaneous business, offset by investment income of ₹1,142 lakhs, less other expenses of ₹335 lakhs = PBT of ₹(4,888) lakhs. As the company is loss-making, no tax provision is recorded, so PBT = PAT.

**Items not disclosed (excluded from table):**
- **Retail health GWP / market share** — the NL-4 Premium Schedule splits GWP only by Health / Personal Accident / Travel segments, not retail vs. group, so this cannot be isolated without estimation.
- **PAT (IFRS) / Claims ratio (IFRS)** — ManipalCigna reports only under Indian GAAP; no IFRS-basis disclosure exists in either the NL filing or Annual Report.

**GWP basis:** ₹410.05 crore represents the statutory Gross Direct Premium as reported in FORM NL-4 — this is the only GWP figure published in this insurer's disclosure format (no separate "ex-1/n" figure exists), so it is reported directly per the "prefer 1/n" sourcing convention.

### Underwriting & Solvency Trends

The **combined ratio of 118%** and **claims ratio of 71%** both indicate continued underwriting losses in Q1FY25 — a deterioration from Q1FY24's 113% combined / 65% claims ratio. This is consistent with the reported operating loss of ₹56.95 crore for the quarter, reflecting elevated claims incidence alongside a still-high commission ratio (21% vs. 15% in the prior-year quarter) as new health/PA business scales.

**Solvency at 1.74x** remains comfortably above the regulatory minimum of 1.50x despite the quarterly loss, aided by fresh capital infusions during the quarter — Share Premium additions of ₹32.93 crore and Capital Contribution of ₹29.11 crore from MEMG Fund Advisors LLP, per Related Party disclosures in the filing.

**Filing date** of 2024-08-14 is derived from the document's timestamp metadata on the company's public disclosure page — the earliest verifiable publication date for the Q1 FY2024-25 NL return set.</ans>
